<title>RUSSIA: Russia may suspend tax payments for power firms.</title>
<headline>Russia may suspend tax payments for power firms.</headline>
<dateline>NOVOSIBIRSK, Russia 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government has offered to suspend federal tax payments for power utilities while debt between the state and the companies is being reconciled, First Deputy Prime Minister Boris Nemtsov said on Monday.</p>
<p>He gave no further details.</p>
<p>Unified Energy System (UES) chairman Boris Brevnov said last week the state owed 13.00 trillion roubles ($2.25 billion) to electricity companies, while the companies owed 5.60 trillion roubles in overdue taxes on July 1, 1997. UES has controlling stakes in the majority of Russia's power companies.</p>
<p>First Deputy Fuel and Energy Minister Sergei Kiriyenko said last week the government would issue three to seven-year bonds to restructure its debt to the firms after reconciliation. ($ = 5,789 roubles)</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
